From 715c4877afb1af80dbc34c0c71d8d1ccd9673599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Louvignes <olivier@mgcrea.io>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:10:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] pwm: add a driver for the Ingenic X1600 PWM controller

The X1600 has a PWM controller of its own, separate from the TCU timers that
pwm-jz4740 drives on earlier Ingenic SoCs: eight channels, each with a
power-of-two clock divider and a waveform word that holds the counts at the
level a period starts with and the counts at the other level. A waveform
word needs at least one count of each level, so a duty cycle of 0 or 100% is
done by switching the channel off with its idle level set accordingly.

The register layout comes from the vendor kernel's driver, as rewritten under
the GPL for HiBy's players.
---
 drivers/pwm/Kconfig             |  11 ++
 drivers/pwm/Makefile            |   1 +
 drivers/pwm/pwm-ingenic-x1600.c | 195 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 207 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/pwm/pwm-ingenic-x1600.c

